# What the evidence has landed in. The class census over the documents that attest to a real
# system.
#
# An empty class here is a finding
#   Every zero is a state the model allows, some relation produces, and no real filing has ever
#   produced. So it is a claim about where the evidence stops rather than about the machinery, and
#   the work it calls for is a document: an entity that files this state, or a measurement that
#   would let one be filed. `reports/classes_in_the_fixtures.sqlc` asks the other half.
-- reports/class_census.sqlc at corpus scope.
:compose(reports/class_census.sqlc, @scope = scope/corpus.sqlc)
